<em>Daring Fireball</em>'s John Gruber <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/10/thoughts_on_new_apple_tv_4k_and_homepod_mini_2">shared his first impressions</a> of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/new-apple-tv-4k-announced/">new Apple TV 4K</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/apple-homepod-mini-2/">HomePod mini 2</a> this week, and he concluded that the price increases the devices received are "much more striking" than any of the new features introduced.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-TV-4K-4th-Generation-Top-View2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070640" /><br/>
Prior to receiving price increases <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/25/apple-tv-and-homepod-price-increases/">in late June</a>, the previous Apple TV 4K started at &#36;129 in the U.S., while the previous HomePod mini was priced at &#36;99. The new Apple TV and the HomePod mini 2 are priced at &#36;299 and &#36;149, respectively, so both devices are now significantly more expensive than they were just four months ago.<br/>
<br/>
Since the new Apple TV is only available in a single configuration with 128GB of storage and an Ethernet port, it is more fair to compare it to the equivalent previous-generation 128GB model, which was initially &#36;149 and went up to &#36;249 in late June. This means the new model is technically only &#36;50 more expensive, but the reality is that the minimum you can spend on a new Apple TV 4K is now &#36;299, up significantly from &#36;129.<br/>
<br/>
The price increases stack up if you want to use a pair of HomePod mini speakers as the default audio output on an Apple TV 4K. As noted by Gruber, it now costs nearly &#36;600 to buy all of those devices, up from nearly &#36;350 before late June.<br/>
<br/>
"At the old pre-June prices, you could buy a 128 GB Apple TV and a pair of HomePod Minis for &#36;350 (&#36;150 + &#36;100 + &#36;100)," said Gruber. "Four short months later, with today's new models, that combination would cost &#36;600 (&#36;300 + &#36;150 + &#36;150). That price difference is much more striking than any of the new and improved features in the products."<br/>
<br/>
